# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Build / packaging
build/
dist/
*.spec.bak

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Local scratch
*.tmp
*.bak
*.log

# Local Claude Code settings (per-machine, not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# **Drawings are never committed, anywhere in the tree.** The designs are the
# maker's own product line — sold, not sample data — so a .gdraw is not ours to
# publish whatever folder it is sitting in. Not root-anchored on purpose: a
# root-anchored rule once let three drawings reach tests/fixtures/ as unpacked
# SVGs. tests/test_no_drawings_committed.py fails if one lands in the index.
#
# Testing against real drawings is still done, by pointing the suite at a
# corpus on disk rather than copying one in: GUILDMODEL_FRAME_CORPUS, or the
# local tests/corpus/ folder, which holds copies of a few library designs
# chosen for the limits they test (see tests/test_frame_corpus.py).
*.gdraw
*.gdraw.bak
*.gmodel
/tests/corpus/

# Whatever lands at the root while something is looked at — a maker's bug
# report and the files that came with it, a program posted for a hand-check,
# reference photos, a teardown or incident note, the maker's planning notes —
# stays local. The app's own images live under docs/ and src/, and the suite's
# reference program under tests/fixtures/, which these root-anchored rules
# leave alone. What was cleared out on 2026-10-15 sits in the dated attic
# beside the repos.
/*.md
!/README.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
/*.txt
!/requirements*.txt
/*.nc
/*.dxf
/*.svg
/*.stl
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/Demo Project*/
/Screenshots/
/demo/
/assets_preview/
src/guildmodel/assets/_iconcache/

# The engineering record: the live plan (/*.md above), its archive and the
# research written for it. Working documents, kept local from v1.5.0; source
# docstrings still cite them by name for anyone who has the tree.
/BUILDPLAN-archive/

# One-shot investigations, each written to answer a single question. Not build
# tooling — scripts/ keeps build_release*, make_icon and dxf_to_stl, which are.
# probe_release_compare.py, the release check, is the one that stays in use.
/scripts/probe_*.py
/scripts/spike_*.py
/scripts/bench_*.py
